{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryReflection","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryInversion"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereFix_isTotallyGeodesic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereFix_isTotallyGeodesic","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L169-L176","doc":"**The hemisphere is totally geodesic** (conditional on the geodesic-\nuniqueness wall) — DERIVED from `dH_boundaryInversion`'s isometry via\n`fixedSet_isTotallyGeodesic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereFix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hemisphereFix","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L164-L167","doc":"The **hemisphere** as the fixed set of a boundary inversion — the Euclidean\nsphere `{‖p - c‖ = R}` centred at the boundary point `c`; its `H³` part is the\nhemisphere Thurston classifies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneFix_isTotallyGeodesic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneFix_isTotallyGeodesic","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L156-L162","doc":"**The vertical plane is totally geodesic** (conditional on the geodesic-\nuniqueness wall) — DERIVED from `dH_verticalReflection`'s isometry via\n`fixedSet_isTotallyGeodesic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneFix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalPlaneFix","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L152-L154","doc":"The **vertical plane** as the fixed set of the vertical reflection — the\nEuclidean plane `{x = 0}` (all heights), a genuine vertical geodesic plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.fixedSet_isTotallyGeodesic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.fixedSet_isTotallyGeodesic","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L114-L148","doc":"**The fixed set of an involutive `dH`-isometry is totally geodesic**\n(conditional on `HypMinimizerUnique`).\n\nGiven `x, y ∈ Fix(φ)` and a minimiser `γ` between them, the image `φ ∘ γ` is again\na minimiser between the same endpoints — `φ` preserves admissibility, length\n(`pathLenH_comp`), and constant speed (`speed_comp`), and fixes `x, y`.  By\nuniqueness `γ t = (φ ∘ γ) t = φ (γ t)`, so `γ t ∈ Fix(φ)`.  A GENUINE conditional\nderivation: it uses the isometry structure and the named uniqueness hypothesis,\nand derives — never assumes — the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HypMinimizerUnique.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HypMinimizerUnique.unique","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HypMinimizerUnique.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HypMinimizerUnique.mk","kind":"ctor","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HypMinimizerUnique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HypMinimizerUnique","kind":"class","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L99-L112","doc":"**THE WALL — geodesic uniqueness in `H³`, an open conjecture.**  Between two\npoints of `H³`, a constant-speed minimiser is unique (pointwise on `[0,1]`).\n\nThis is the one genuinely open, Mathlib-scale input of the whole T2 development.\nIt is axiomatised as a `class` with a **content-bearing** field — a real\n`∀`-quantified equality, the honest uniqueness proposition — and is deliberately\ngiven **NO instance**: the open state is a content-bearing carrier with no\nwitness, per AGENTS.md §3b-tax.  It is a *primary* conjecture (no other\nconjecture class appears in its signature).  Existence of minimisers is part of\nthe same wall and is likewise not asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsTotallyGeodesic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsTotallyGeodesic","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L92-L97","doc":"**Totally geodesic** (minimiser-convexity form): every minimiser between two\npoints of `S` has its whole segment `γ([0,1])` inside `S`.  This is the only form\nstatable without a Riemannian second fundamental form; it is exactly the property\nthe classification proves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.constSpeed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.constSpeed","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.minimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.minimal","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.admissible","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsHypMinimizer","kind":"structure","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L84-L90","doc":"**A constant-speed length-minimiser** from `x` to `y`: an admissible path of\nminimal hyperbolic length whose speed is constant along `[0,1]`.  Constant speed\nis the canonical (geodesic) parametrisation — see the file header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hypSpeed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hypSpeed","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesic.lean#L80-L82","doc":"**Hyperbolic (local) speed** of a path `γ` at `t`: the line element `‖γ'‖/z`\nwhose integral is `pathLenH`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}